# Changesets

Every user-visible change (feature, bug fix, breaking change, notable behavior change) needs a changeset via `pnpm changeset`.

## Required

- Add a changeset in the same change set as the code (patch / minor / major as appropriate)
- Describe the impact for consumers, not implementation detail
- Do not bump `package.json` version by hand

## Exception — unreleased work

If the change only fixes or adjusts a **new feature that is not released yet** and already has an open changeset under `.changeset/`, do **not** add another changeset. Fold the fix into that pending release note if the wording should change.

```text
✅ Feature landed with a changeset → later bug in that unreleased feature → no new changeset
✅ Bug in already-released behavior → new patch changeset
✅ New feature / public API change → new changeset
```

## Skip

Internal-only work with no consumer impact (refactors, tests, lint, docs-only, tooling) does not need a changeset unless it affects the published package or documented API.
